# Audi A6 C4 four-door saloon, 1994-1997.
#
# The first A6: the C4 platform with the rounded Audi 100-derived body, the
# four-ring grille and the quattro option. The Avant is a different body and
# is not represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audi_A6
#
# Dimensions 4.797 x 1.783 x 1.430 m, wheelbase 2.692 m (quattro).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a near-level broadside of a C4 quattro; the
# front and rear three-quarters show the lamps and tail.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK chart was established. Black, silver, grey and
# blue are plain names. Weights 18, 16, 14, 12, total 60, provisional.
#
# Speed 220 km/h. Comfort 85/458, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 85. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1994 intro, retires staggered 2017-2020.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/audi-a6-c4.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/audi-a6-c4.dae. References:
# citycars/references/audi-a6-c4/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the wheels are plain discs without the six-spoke pattern,
# the tail lamps are rectangular blocks without the chrome divider, and the
# headlamps read weakly against a pale body. The family shape is simplified, and
# the rear window is more upright than the photograph's. At 128 px the upright
# C-pillar, rectangular lamps and narrow ringed grille read as a C4 A6.


obj=citycar
name=AudiA6C4(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=18
